WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.340
The start of spooky season is right around
the corner but first, our favorite streaming

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:09.000
services need to let go of some titles to
make way for new content, and Netflix is no

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:09.720
exception.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:13.720
These are the movies you won't want to miss
out on before they leave Netflix in October

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:14.720
2019.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:20.100
The brilliant minds of Steven Spielberg and
Stanley Kubrick come together in A.I.

00:00:20.109 --> 00:00:26.269
Artificial Intelligence, the 2001 sci-fi drama
Kubrick began developing in the late 1970s,

00:00:26.269 --> 00:00:31.640
venturing to adapt Brian Aldiss' short story
"Super-Toys Last All Summer Long" into a feature

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:32.420
film.

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:38.080
In 1985, Kubrick teamed with Spielberg to
continue crafting the project, and when Kubrick

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:42.220
handed Spielberg the directorial reins a decade
later, he ran away with it.

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:47.180
What ended up on the silver screen was the
unique story of a childlike robot named David,

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:52.600
played by Haley Joel Osment, whose ability
to love and abandonment by his adoptive parents

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:54.940
set him on a journey to become a real boy.

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:59.960
It's one part The Adventures of Pinocchio,
one part The Wizard of Oz, and one part exploration

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:02.580
of a future, post-climate change world.

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:08.579
It's also got Jude Law as a male prostitute
named Gigolo Joe, so there really isn't anything

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:10.000
more you could want from A.I.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:13.780
"I've picked up a lot of business in this
spot."

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.960
With two equally mind-boggling sci-fi horror
sequels having come out in the last three

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:27.840
years, it can be hard to remember where the
Cloverfield franchise actually began.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:33.859
It started in 2008, before Dan Trachtenberg
pulled a last-minute twist in 10 Cloverfield

00:01:33.859 --> 00:01:38.869
Lane and prior to Netflix's surprise release
of The Cloverfield Paradox, with the original

00:01:38.869 --> 00:01:41.980
found-footage thriller helmed by Matt Reeves.

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:47.080
Cloverfield takes its name from the fictional
case in the movie known as "Cloverfield,"

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:51.350
an incident in which an enormous parasitic
creature and a horde of smaller monsters run

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:54.920
rampant through New York City, killing people
and destroying the city.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:59.060
Presented as video clips that members of the
U.S. Department of Defense recovered from

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:03.990
a camcorder located in what was once Central
Park, the film follows a group of friends

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:08.020
as they attempt to evade the monsters and
make it out of the Big Apple alive.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:11.440
Spoiler alert: Not all are successful in that
endeavor.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:14.300
Cloverfield will remain on Netflix until October
1.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:20.560
The stoner movie that might define all stoner
movies, Pineapple Express will sadly be leaving

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:21.980
Netflix before you know it.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:26.200
Until that time comes, however, squeeze in
one more viewing of the buddy action-comedy

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:31.600
centered on a lazy stoner named Dale, his
dazed-and-confused dealer Saul, and his supplier

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:36.390
Red as they flee from hitmen and gangsters
after witnessing a drug lord and a crooked

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:38.860
police officer kill a man in cold blood.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:43.800
Pineapple Express' silliness is what makes
the David Gordon Green-directed film so enjoyable.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:48.571
It's made even better by all-in performances
from the whole cast particularly Franco, who

00:02:48.571 --> 00:02:53.490
nabbed a Golden Globe nomination for his work
as Saul and a wonderfully quotable script

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:56.840
from Rogen and his longtime creative partner
Evan Goldberg.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.100
"Only reason I started selling pot is so I
could put my bubbe in a nice retirement home."

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:05.020
Catch a ride on the Pineapple Express on Netflix
until October 1.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:10.060
For horror lovers, October is the time to
watch at least one of the films in the Scream

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:12.120
franchise at least once per week.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:18.160
Get a head start on that annual tradition
by working backwards with Scream 4, the 2011

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:22.020
franchise-closer that takes place during the
15th anniversary of the Woodsboro murders

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:24.260
from the original 1996 movie.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:26.360
"What do you think?"

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:28.760
"Well, I guess today is the anniversary.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:30.220
Kids."

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:35.980
Directed by slasher film icon Wes Craven,
Scream 4 sees Sidney Prescott returning to

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:40.300
Woodsboro with her publicist Rebecca Walters
as part of the tour to promote her new self-help

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:41.200
book.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:45.640
Sidney gets a lot more than she bargained
for, of course, as she soon becomes a suspect

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:46.920
in a number of killings.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:52.340
Things go from bad to worse when the masked
killer Ghostface begins calling Sidney's cousin

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:53.980
Jill and threatening her life.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:59.360
As Sidney and Jill attempt to crack the case,
so too do Woodsboro sheriff Dewey Riley and

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:01.100
his wife Gale Weathers-Riley.

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:06.480
It's a fight against time, circumstance, and
traumatic history to rid Woodsboro of Ghostface

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:11.120
for good and Netflix subscribers have until
October 7 to find out how it all ends.

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:17.720
Directed by Norwegian filmmaker Morten Tyldum
and based on the Andrew Hodges-written biography

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:23.370
Alan Turing: The Enigma, 2014's The Imitation
Game tells the incredible true-life story

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:28.400
of British cryptanalyst Alan Turing, who worked
as part of the British government's cryptography

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:33.740
team during World War II and decrypted the
thought-to-be-unbreakable German codes transmitted

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:35.660
by the country's Enigma machine.

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:40.400
Throughout the course of the film, it's revealed
that Turing is gay, which was punishable by

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:45.080
law in England at the time and complicates
Turing's personal and professional lives.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:50.080
The end of The Imitation Game will stir even
the steeliest of people leaving little question

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:55.780
as to why the film won an Academy Award in
2015, or why critics have praised it as, quote,

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:58.140
"a moving tribute to an extraordinary man."

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:02.260
The Imitation Game is available to stream
on Netflix until October 29.

